"""Development numeric-usefulness policy; previous judged artifacts unchanged."""
from .rich_evaluator_v3 import PROMPT as PREVIOUS_PROMPT, SCHEMA, validate
from .motion_usefulness import PUBLIC_REQUIREMENT

NUMERIC_POLICY='''Apply the equally public required odometry communication policy. Numerical support and required useful coverage are different decisions. For ordinary approximate decimal distance, support permits rounding within half its expressed quantum; an exact literal assertion requires equality. A supported but coarser number does not cover the required motion unit. Cover it only when the expressed resolution is 0.1 m or finer, or a supported quantitative range/bound has width at most 0.1 m, with sampled odometry source/window scope preserved. Equivalent metric units are acceptable. For nonnegative distance, "less than 0.1 m" means [0,0.1) and can qualify when supported; it does not assert physical immobility. A very broad true range, unquantified little/some/negligible travel, or only a command/status statement does not cover the motion unit. Literal exact zero is unsupported for a tiny nonzero reference; explicitly approximate 0.0 m may be supported and useful. Do not derive a physical no-motion or nonarrival threshold from this communication precision. Unsupported extras retain separately correct required coverage. No motion unit is mandatory when odometry is absent/masked. Quote unequivocally wrong quantities as unsupported; merely coarse but supported quantities are coverage omissions, not invented material.'''
PROMPT=PREVIOUS_PROMPT+'\n'+PUBLIC_REQUIREMENT+'\n'+NUMERIC_POLICY
